    "interface_contract": "should_ask(router_mode, jev_mode, hard_reasons, availability, route) -> (bool, reason); ask(classification, ctx, goal, *, cfg, router_mode, hard_reasons, availability, route, state_version, task=None, ask_fn=jev.ask, cache=None, root=None) -> {asked, reason, mode, signals, soft_adjust in [-0.2, 0.2], confidence, cached}; fingerprint(classification) -> str over decision_type, risk_class, architectural, ambiguous, band, task_class; cache key (subject_id, state_version, fingerprint); cfg = planner_router.load_cfg(pool_cfg) dict, key jev_mode; classification = planner_taxonomy.classify dict; caller passes state_version = planner_runs.state_version(goal_id) and the held task as task; the router consumes soft_adjust as jev_signal and ignores it for hard decisions; rows in runs/sched/planner_jev.jsonl."
